You are tasked with implementing a C++ class that encodes reachability into an Answer Set Programming (ASP) program. The class, named ASP, is responsible for generating an ASP program that represents the reachability of nodes in a graph. The graph is represented by the AN class, which is provided in the "../model/AN.hpp" header file.

Your task is to complete the implementation of the ASP class by adding a method that generates an ASP program representing the reachability of nodes in the given graph. The ASP program should encode the reachability information in a format suitable for ASP solvers to determine the reachability of nodes in the graph.

You are provided with the following incomplete class definition for ASP:

```cpp
#include "../model/AN.hpp"

class ASP {
public:
    // Constructor and other methods are not shown for brevity

    /*!
     * \brief Generate an ASP program representing the reachability of nodes in the given graph.
     * \param graph The graph for which reachability is to be encoded.
     * \return A string containing the ASP program representing the reachability of nodes in the graph.
     */
    std::string generateReachabilityASP(const AN& graph);
};
```

You need to implement the `generateReachabilityASP` method to generate the ASP program representing the reachability of nodes in the given graph.

```cpp
#include <sstream>

std::string ASP::generateReachabilityASP(const AN& graph) {
    std::stringstream aspProgram;

    // Add ASP rules to encode reachability
    for (int sourceNode = 0; sourceNode < graph.getNumNodes(); ++sourceNode) {
        for (int targetNode = 0; targetNode < graph.getNumNodes(); ++targetNode) {
            if (graph.isReachable(sourceNode, targetNode)) {
                aspProgram << "reachable(" << sourceNode << ", " << targetNode << ").\n";
            } else {
                aspProgram << ":- not reachable(" << sourceNode << ", " << targetNode << ").\n";
            }
        }
    }

    return aspProgram.str();
}
```

In the solution, the `generateReachabilityASP` method iterates through all pairs of nodes in the graph and encodes their reachability using ASP rules. For each pair of nodes, if the `isReachable` method of the AN class returns true, the ASP rule `reachable(sourceNode, targetNode)` is added to the ASP program. If the nodes are not reachable, a constraint `:- not reachable(sourceNode, targetNode)` is added to the ASP program. The method returns the generated ASP program as a string.

You are tasked with implementing a function that reads data from a file stream and handles potential exceptions. The function should read a specified number of bytes from the file stream into a buffer and return the number of bytes actually read. If an exception occurs during the read operation, the function should return an appropriate error code.

You are given the following code snippet as a reference:

```cpp
return STG_E_INVALIDPOINTER;

ULONG read = 0;
try
{
    this->mRstream.read(static_cast<char *>(_pv), _cb);
    read = static_cast<ULONG>(this->mRstream.gcount());
}
catch (const std::ios_base::failure &)
{
