The `nvector::Read<I2Point>(3)` function reads three 2D points from the input and stores them in the `vp` vector. You need to use these points to determine if they are collinear.

A set of 3 points is collinear if the slope of the line formed by any two points is the same as the slope of the line formed by the other two points.

