```cpp
int lca(int a, int b) {
    if (lv[a] < lv[b]) swap(a, b);
    int log = 1;
    while ((1 << log) <= lv[a]) log++;
    log--;

    for (int i = log; i >= 0; i--) {
        if (lv[a] - (1 << i) >= lv[b]) {
            a = dp[i][a];
        }
    }

    if (a == b) return a;

    for (int i = log; i >= 0; i--) {
        if (dp[i][a] != dp[i][b]) {
            a = dp[i][a];
            b = dp[i][b];
        }
    }

    return dp[0][a];
}
```

In the `lca` function, we first ensure that node `a` is at a higher level than node `b`. Then, we find the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to the level of node `a`. We use this to move node `a` up the tree to the same level as node `b`. Then, we move both nodes up the tree in lockstep until they have the same parent, which is the lowest common ancestor.

