Your task is to implement the `projected_area` function to calculate the total projected area of all triangles in the `tlist` onto the plane with the normal `pn`. The projected area of a triangle onto a plane is the area of the triangle when projected onto the plane perpendicular to the plane's normal.

You should assume that the necessary functions for calculating the area of a triangle and projecting a point onto a plane are available.

Write a function `double projected_area(Vector3d &pn, TriangleList &tlist)` that returns the total projected area of the triangles onto the specified plane.

```cpp
#include <cmath>

// Function to calculate the area of a triangle given its vertices
double triangle_area(const Vector3d &p1, const Vector3d &p2, const Vector3d &p3) {
    double a = sqrt(pow(p2.x - p1.x, 2) + pow(p2.y - p1.y, 2) + pow(p2.z - p1.z, 2));
    double b = sqrt(pow(p3.x - p2.x, 2) + pow(p3.y - p2.y, 2) + pow(p3.z - p2.z, 2));
    double c = sqrt(pow(p1.x - p3.x, 2) + pow(p1.y - p3.y, 2) + pow(p1.z - p3.z, 2));
    double s = (a + b + c) / 2;
    return sqrt(s * (s - a) * (s - b) * (s - c));
}

// Function to project a point onto a plane given the point and the plane's normal
Vector3d project_point(const Vector3d &point, const Vector3d &pn) {
    double d = (point.x * pn.x + point.y * pn.y + point.z * pn.z) / (pn.x * pn.x + pn.y * pn.y + pn.z * pn.z);
    Vector3d projected_point;
    projected_point.x = point.x - d * pn.x;
    projected_point.y = point.y - d * pn.y;
    projected_point.z = point.z - d * pn.z;
    return projected_point;
}

// Function to calculate the projected area of a triangle onto a plane
double projected_area(Vector3d &pn, TriangleList &tlist) {
    double total_area = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < tlist.n_triangles; i++) {
        Vector3d p1 = project_point(tlist.triangles[i].p[0], pn);
        Vector3d p2 = project_point(tlist.triangles[i].p[1], pn);
        Vector3d p3 = project_point(tlist.triangles[i].p[2], pn);
        total_area += triangle_area(p1, p2, p3);
    }
    return total_area;
}
```

The `projected_area` function first projects each vertex of every triangle onto the specified plane using the `project_point` function. Then, it calculates the area of the projected triangle using the `triangle_area` function and accumulates the total area. Finally, it returns the total projected area of all triangles onto the specified plane.

