You are tasked with implementing a dependency resolution algorithm for a software application. The application is composed of modules, each with its own dependencies and initialization logic. The provided code snippet is a part of the application framework and includes a method to retrieve the dependencies of a module and an initialization method for the application.

Your task is to create a function that, given a list of modules and their dependencies, resolves the initialization order of the modules based on their dependencies. The function should return a list of module IDs in the order in which they should be initialized.

The `Application::dependsOn()` method returns the dependencies of a module as a vector of `ModuleId`. The `Application::init()` method initializes the application and returns a `uint8_t` status code.

You need to implement the following function:
```cpp
std::vector<ModuleId> resolveInitializationOrder(const std::vector<Module>& modules);
```

The `Module` class is defined as follows:
```cpp
class Module {
public:
    ModuleId id;
    std::vector<ModuleId> dependencies;
};
```

Your task is to implement the `resolveInitializationOrder` function to determine the correct order in which the modules should be initialized based on their dependencies. If there are multiple valid initialization orders, return any one of them.

Example:
Given the following modules and their dependencies:
```
Module A: dependencies = {}
Module B: dependencies = {A}
Module C: dependencies = {A, B}
Module D: dependencies = {B}
```
The correct initialization order would be: A, B, D, C.

```cpp
#include <vector>
#include <unordered_map>
#include <queue>

std::vector<ModuleId> resolveInitializationOrder(const std::vector<Module>& modules) {
    std::unordered_map<ModuleId, std::vector<ModuleId>> dependencyMap;
    std::unordered_map<ModuleId, int> dependencyCount;

    for (const auto& module : modules) {
        dependencyMap[module.id] = module.dependencies;
        dependencyCount[module.id] = module.dependencies.size();
    }

    std::vector<ModuleId> initializationOrder;
    std::queue<ModuleId> moduleQueue;

    for (const auto& module : modules) {
        if (module.dependencies.empty()) {
            moduleQueue.push(module.id);
            initializationOrder.push_back(module.id);
        }
    }

    while (!moduleQueue.empty()) {
        ModuleId currentModule = moduleQueue.front();
        moduleQueue.pop();

        for (const auto& [moduleId, dependencies] : dependencyMap) {
            for (const auto& dependency : dependencies) {
                if (dependency == currentModule) {
                    dependencyCount[moduleId]--;
                    if (dependencyCount[moduleId] == 0) {
                        moduleQueue.push(moduleId);
                        initializationOrder.push_back(moduleId);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }

    return initializationOrder;
}
```

